---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="lead">
      Choose the kind of help you need, pick a time, and we will confirm it by
      email. If you would rather talk to someone first,
      <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}?text=Hello%2C%20I%27d%20like%20some%20help%20with%20an%20IT%20problem" target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us on WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      or <a href="/quote/">ask us to call you back</a> instead.
    </p>
    <h2>Why we ask for a booking fee</h2>
    <p>
      Holding a slot means turning someone else away, and driving to a job
      that isn't there costs us the afternoon. The £{{ site.bookingFee }} is a
      small check that a booking is real — it is not meant to cover our time,
      just to make sure someone is expecting us.
    </p>
    <p>
      It isn't an extra charge — it comes off your first hour, and you get it
      back in full if we can't fix the problem. Our
      <a href="/booking-terms/">booking terms</a> set out the details.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We never see your card details.</strong> Payment is handled by
      Stripe, our payment provider. Nothing is stored by us.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{# The calendar is Microsoft Bookings, embedded so customers stay on our site.
   It is a third-party frame, so two things are deliberate:
   - loading="lazy" keeps it off the critical path; the page text renders first
   - the fallback link below is NOT optional. Some browsers block third-party
     cookies inside frames, and when that happens the calendar simply fails to
     load with no error the customer understands. Without a way out they cannot
     book and will not tell us why. #}
<section class="section booking-embed-section">
  <div class="container">
    <iframe
      class="booking-embed"
      src="{{ site.bookingUrl }}"
      title="Booking calendar — choose a service and time"
      loading="lazy"></iframe>

    <p class="booking-fallback">
      Calendar not loading?
      <a href="{{ site.bookingUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the booking page in a new tab<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>,
      or just
      <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us on WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      and we will book it for you.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
